      "years": [2015, 2022],
      "pattern": "drift",
      "direction": "increase",
      "magnitude": "~+0.13 peak deviation (~+0.013/yr), z up to +4.6",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "evidence": [
        "3y MA rises steadily from 0.96 to 1.08 (R²=0.83); 7y consecutive upward run (+0.176); 2022-2023 excursion score 9.6; mild overdispersion (x2.32) keeps Poisson null valid for individual z-scores. 2024 reversion to 0.976 noted but does not negate the prior sustained build-up."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate CI incidence drivers (underwriting criteria changes, medical coding updates, product mix shifts, or morbidity trends). Review pricing and valuation assumptions for CI. Monitor 2024-2025 experience to determine if the reversion indicates normalization or a return to baseline volatility."
    }
  ]
}

